# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Git on Windows checks text files out as CRLF by default. Two things in this
# repository break when it does:
#
#   * The layout fixtures are compared *byte for byte* against what the
#     exporter produces, and the exporter emits `\n`. A CRLF checkout fails
#     `every_fixture_round_trips_byte_for_byte` on Windows only.
#   * The packaging scripts run under Git Bash. A `.sh` file with CRLF endings
#     fails with a "bad interpreter" error naming a path that looks correct,
#     which is among the more baffling ways to lose an afternoon.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png           binary
*.ico           binary
*.icns          binary
*.pdf           binary
*.gz            binary
*.tgz           binary
*.7z            binary
*.zip           binary
*.dmg           binary
*.exe           binary
*.dll           binary
*.so            binary
*.dylib         binary
